      "writtenOn": "2022-11-14T11:18:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Blocks are re-created lazily on first access and not on this code path. The `force_pte\u003dtrue` mechanism was here before coalescing and I don\u0027t see how it changes semantics because I only extend the current functionality with this.\n\nThe second concern is true but I raised this up with @qperret@google.com before implementing this. It turns out it is not the only place where we are making this assumption: (eg. take a look on the pkvm reclaim path).\n\nI explored your suggested option as we discussed together on Friday: relying on the anchor which is set in _PRE to re-create the block mappings in _POST in `stage2_map_walk_leaf`. This will involve setting `force_pte\u003dfalse` on the `kvm_pgtable_stage2_set_owner` path but this API is also invoked from hyp and guest. One issue is that it will not invalidated caches on this path.",
      "parentUuid": "dc08581f_b213c3a2",
      "revId": "610298ba7fc9ee1de6399cd85fb16eeeaddb5a32",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
